#### Phase 1 — Curvature-Based Severity Features

##### [MODIFY] [features.py](file:///c:/Users/honpa/Desktop/programming/Pothole%20Detection/Vision-Based-Pothole-Detection/features.py)

Add 4 new functions below all existing functions (no existing code modified):

1. **`extract_curvature_features(mask)`** — Returns dict with 10 curvature features:
   - `max_curvature`, `mean_curvature`, `std_curvature`, `p90_curvature` (from absolute curvature profile)
   - `curvature_entropy` (from normalized distribution)
   - `high_curvature_fraction` (fraction > mean + 1 std)
   - `concave_fraction` (negative signed curvature points)
   - `curvature_sign_changes` (boundary irregularity)
   - `contour_length`, `contour_elongation`
   - Uses `scipy.signal.savgol_filter` for smoothing

2. **`extract_depth_profile_features(mask, depth_map, n_slices=8)`** — Returns dict with 5 features:
   - `mean_bowl_depth`, `max_bowl_depth`, `std_bowl_depth`
   - `mean_road_curvature`, `slope_variance`
   - Novel: fits quadratic to road surface outside mask, extrapolates expected depth at center

3. **`extract_surface_normal_features(depth_map, mask, neighborhood_size=15)`** — Returns dict with 4 features:
   - `mean_normal_deviation`, `max_normal_deviation`, `std_normal_deviation`, `p90_normal_deviation`
   - Computes angular deviation of boundary normals from road reference normal

4. **`extract_all_geometry_features(mask, depth_map, image_rgb=None)`** — Combines all 3 above into single dict (~19 new features total). Handles None returns gracefully.

